# The product's deployed name: the one place it is set (PO, 2026-10-31). It drives every cluster-visible name of a render
# (namespaces `<product>`, `<product>-build`, `<product>-security`; PriorityClasses; ServiceAccounts, Services, PVCs,
# Secrets and ConfigMaps whose name carries it; the `app.kubernetes.io/part-of` label; the in-cluster registry
# repositories `<product>-dataplane`, `<product>-control`), through tools/pilot/render.py, tools/deploy/manifest_check.py
# and the tools/pilot scripts. The committed manifests are written with `rwsafe`; the render renames them.
# Application-internal identifiers (environment variable names, mount paths, Secret keys, database and role names, the
# snapshot key id) keep their names. A shell may override it for one command: `PRODUCT=<name> tools/pilot/...`.
# Rules (manifest_check.validate_product): lower case, 2-20 characters, never a neXus or Kubernetes name.
PRODUCT=rwsafe
